WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:07.465
Each step maps to NIST SP 800-53 controls,
to FedRAMP Key Security Indicators

2
00:00:07.465 --> 00:00:12.100
where the workbook already pairs them,
and to the evidence the ISSO keeps.

3
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.689
The partner entry and its trust
settings support AC-3, AC-20 and IA-8,

4
00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:23.900
with test zero's output and the
agreement clause behind each trust value.

5
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.049
The access package, its approval
and expiry support AC-2,

6
00:00:28.049 --> 00:00:31.075
with the policy export and review history.

7
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:35.263
Suspension, removal and exit
support automated account disabling,

8
00:00:35.263 --> 00:00:39.900
and stand in for the agency's own
personnel controls through the agreement.

9
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.088
Denial and MFA tests
support IA-8 and IA-2.

10
00:00:45.088 --> 00:00:50.012
Monitoring supports AU-6,
and drift supports CA-7.

11
00:00:50.012 --> 00:00:54.532
Key Security Indicators describe
what cloud service providers report,

12
00:00:54.532 --> 00:00:58.900
so the agency doesn't report them; it
lines its own evidence up with them.

13
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.189
And the cloud services involved
must sit inside a FedRAMP-certified

14
00:01:03.189 --> 00:01:06.720
offering that the agency's
own authorization relies on.
